  m_Name: tulip
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::FlowerData
  id: tulip
  displayName: Tulip
  scientificName: Tulipa gesneriana
  markerImageName: tulip
  description: The garden tulip is a bulbous perennial valued for its elegant, cup-shaped
    flowers and wide variety of colours and forms. A single upright stem usually
    carries one prominent flower above broad, blue-green leaves. Most modern garden
    tulips belong to cultivated groups developed through centuries of selection and
    hybridisation.
  origin: Cultivated form historically associated with Turkey; tulips as a group
    originate across parts of Europe, North Africa and Central and Western Asia
  meaning: Perfect love, elegance and renewal. Red tulips represent deep or true
    love, yellow tulips represent happiness, white tulips represent forgiveness,
    purple tulips represent royalty and pink tulips represent affection and good
    wishes.
  habitat: Open grasslands, rocky mountain slopes, steppes and cultivated gardens
    with fertile, well-drained soil.
  birthflower: April, in many modern birth-flower traditions
  floweringSeason: March to May, depending on the cultivar and climate
  sunlight: Full sun is best. Provide at least six hours of direct sunlight for strong
    stems and good flowering.
  watering: Water after planting and keep the soil lightly moist during active spring
    growth. Avoid excessive watering or permanently wet soil, as the bulbs can rot.
    Reduce watering after the foliage turns yellow and the bulb enters dormancy.
  difficulty: Easy to Moderate
  arScale: 0.05
  flowerImage: {fileID: 0}
